{"tool_name":"mitotox","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"mitotox","home":"http://www.mitotox.org","license":"CC-BY-NC-4.0","summary":"A comprehensive mitochondrial toxicity database.","addition_date":"2021-12-02T16:53:45.191623Z","last_update_date":"2021-12-02T16:54:49.117241Z","tool_type":["Database portal","Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:mitotox","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"acwei86@ntu.edu.tw","name":"An-Chi Wei","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7927-1636","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Chi-Jung Huang"},{"name":"Ko-Hong Lin"},{"name":"Yu-Te Lin"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://www.mitotox.org/about/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Database search","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2421"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"},{"term":"Subcellular localisation prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2489"}]}],"name":"MitoTox","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/S12859-021-04285-3","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).Background: Mitochondria play essential roles in regulating cellular functions. Some drug treatments and molecular interventions have been reported to have off-target effects damaging mitochondria and causing severe side effects. The development of a database for the management of mitochondrial toxicity-related molecules and their targets is important for further analyses. Results: To correlate chemical, biological and mechanistic information on clinically relevant mitochondria-related toxicity, a comprehensive mitochondrial toxicity database (MitoTox) was developed. MitoTox is an electronic repository that integrates comprehensive information about mitochondria-related toxins and their targets. Information and data related to mitochondrial toxicity originate from various sources, including scientific journals and other electronic databases. These resources were manually verified and extracted into MitoTox. The database currently contains over 1400 small-molecule compounds, 870 mitochondrial targets, and more than 4100 mitochondrial toxin-target associations. Each MitoTox data record contains over 30 fields, including biochemical properties, therapeutic classification, target proteins, toxicological data, mechanistic information, clinical side effects, and references. Conclusions: MitoTox provides a fully searchable database with links to references and other databases. Potential applications of MitoTox include toxicity classification, prediction, reference and education. MitoTox is available online at http://www.mitotox.org.","authors":[{"name":"Huang C.-J."},{"name":"Lin K.-H."},{"name":"Lin Y.-T."},{"name":"Wei A.-C."}],"date":"2021-05-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"BMC Bioinformatics","title":"MitoTox: a comprehensive mitochondrial toxicity database"},"pmcid":"PMC8283953","pmid":"34266386"}],"topic":[{"term":"Cell biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2229"},{"term":"Drug discovery","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3336"},{"term":"Pharmacology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0202"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"},{"term":"Toxicology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2840"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"MitoTox","home":"https://bio.tools/mitotox","license":"CC-BY-NC-4.0","summary":"A comprehensive mitochondrial toxicity database.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:mitotox/db/www.mitotox.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":false},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":24,"citation